{
  "info": {
    "name": "RecruitFlow API",
    "_postman_id": "b1a7c0de-0000-4a00-9000-recruitflow01",
    "description": "Full RecruitFlow ATS workflow: candidate self-registration, stateless JWT auth with refresh tokens & logout, autocomplete candidate search & profiles, jobs with role + object-level ownership security, and the application pipeline with department-level security and auditing (updatedBy/updatedAt).\n\nHOW TO USE:\n1. Start the app (http://localhost:8080) and MongoDB (docker compose up -d).\n2. Run the requests top-to-bottom, or use the Collection Runner.\n3. Login/Register requests save tokens into collection variables automatically; later requests reuse them. Login - Recruiter also saves {{refreshToken}}. Create Job saves {{jobId}}; Apply saves {{appId}}.\n\nToken lifecycle: the access token (\"token\") is short-lived (~15 min); use Refresh Token to get a new one, and Logout to revoke the refresh token.\n\nDemo users (seeded by DataSeeder): admin/admin, recruiter/recruiter, recruiter2/recruiter2 (second recruiter, for job-ownership tests), candidate/candidate, eng_manager/eng_manager (Engineering), mkt_manager/mkt_manager (Marketing). Registered users are always CANDIDATE.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "recruiterToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "candidateToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "engManagerToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "mktManagerToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "newCandidateToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "recruiter2Token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "deleteJobId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "jobId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "appId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
